            <div xml:id="d239-a8">

                <pb facs="0348" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg242"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No. 237.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Medical report of Dr. S. S. White</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Valparaiso</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-11-20"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. B. McCreery</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Consul, Valparaiso</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In obedience to orders from Capt. Schley,
                    on November 3, 1891, I examined Patrick Shields, a fireman belonging to the
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Keweenaw</hi>, and found his condition to be as
                    follows: A severe contusion on back of head, a small cut over right <pb
                        facs="0349" n="243" xml:id="pg243"/> eye, and his body severely bruised,
                    both front and back, from nape of neck to end of spine, of such severity as to
                    render him unfit for duty for several weeks.</p>
                <p>His condition now is somewhat improved, but his nervous system has sustained a
                    shock from which months will be necessary for recovery, if he is ever as
                    physically sound as he was at the time he received the injury.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stephen S. White</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Passed Assistant Surgeon, U. S.
                    Navy</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">U. S. S.
                                Baltimore</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">First
                            Rate</hi>).</dateline></opener>
                    <p>Approved and forwarded.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. S. Schley</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Captain Commanding</hi>.</signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
